      faqs: [{"q":"What is an images to pdf converter?","a":"An images to pdf converter is a tool that takes image files, such as JPG, PNG, or WebP pictures, and combines them into a single PDF document. Each image normally becomes one page, in the order you arrange them. The result is a file that opens on any device, prints at a fixed page size, and is easy to share as one attachment."},{"q":"Which image formats can I convert to PDF?","a":"The UtilityFlow converter accepts JPG, PNG, and WebP images. JPG suits photographs, PNG suits screenshots and diagrams with sharp text, and WebP suits images downloaded from websites. If your image is in another format, such as BMP, TIFF, or HEIC, convert it to JPG or PNG first before adding it to the PDF."},{"q":"Should I choose A4, US Letter, or fit to image?","a":"Choose A4 if the PDF will be printed or filed in most of the world, and US Letter if the recipient is in the United States or Canada. Choose Exact Image Dimensions, or fit to image, when the PDF will only be read on a screen, when your images have mixed orientations, or when you want each image shown at its natural size."},{"q":"Are my images uploaded to a server when I convert them?","a":"Not with the UtilityFlow converter. It runs entirely in your browser using pdf-lib, so your images stay on your device while the PDF is built and the finished file is downloaded directly. Nothing is uploaded or stored on a server, which makes it a safer choice for personal documents such as identity papers and receipts."},{"q":"Can an images to pdf converter make blurry photos sharp?","a":"No. A converter places your images into a PDF exactly as they are, so a blurry, dark, or badly angled original will look the same in the PDF. Always check each image at full size before converting, and retake any page that is hard to read. The converter packages your images, it does not improve them."},{"q":"Can I convert images to PDF on my phone?","a":"Yes. The converter runs in your browser, so it works on a phone, a tablet, or a computer without installing an app. Select the photos from your camera roll, arrange them in order, choose a page size, and download the finished PDF. Fit to image is often the best page size choice for phone photos viewed on screen."}],
